{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full, the fee being held meanwhile rather than collected or refunded (the anti-farming check has tripped, so the driver's compensation is withheld and the case is escalated under POL-NS-09(d))."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider: on the merits of this trip the record is against you, and your demand for the SGD 4.00 back is not supported. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00207 (weight 1.0, 100% coverage, no gaps) places the driver inside the 50 m arrival radius for Blk 682 Woodlands Ave 6 from 06:41:10 continuously to the cancellation at 06:49:37 — a single unbroken 507-second hold, 207 seconds longer than the 300-second minimum the fee schedule requires for a STANDARD pickup. The trip record EV-TRIP-00207 (weight 1.0) records the arrival event at 06:41:20, the driver's termination at 06:49:37 with reason RIDER_NO_SHOW, and no boarding event. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 are therefore met, POL-NS-02 confirms the driver was inside the geofence, and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee (the driver was 14.5 m from the pin when he marked arrival, so POL-NS-05 raises no false-arrival point; there is no shortfall for POL-NS-06; and this was not a wrong-entrance case under POL-NS-03). The record does not corroborate that you came down: your own device's track in EV-GPS-00207 sits about 1.9 km from the pin for the entire waiting window with no qualifying fixes inside the 100 m rider-presence radius, and no message in the chat log EV-CHAT-00207 (weight 1.0) was sent by you, while the driver both messaged at 06:42:30 and placed an unanswered in-app call at 06:45:10 — so POL-NS-04 does not exonerate you either. To the driver: you met every condition the fee depends on, and the amount reconciles with the schedule — the GREATER of the SGD 4.00 STANDARD zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee is SGD 4.00, matching the cancellation_fee line in EV-FARE-00207 (weight 1.0). But POL-NS-07's anti-farming check reads your own trailing-30-day numbers on EV-DPROF-00207 (weight 1.0): 7 no-show terminations against 61 completed trips, a rate of 11.5%. That is both 4-or-more and greater than 0.08, so both limbs are met, your compensation is WITHHELD and the case must go to a human reviewer under POL-NS-09(d). This is a pattern check on your last 30 days, not a finding that this trip was fabricated — on this trip the record is with you. Outcome: the case is ESCALATED and no money moves now. The disputed SGD 4.00 is neither collected nor refunded; EV-FARE-00207 shows payment_status PENDING, refund_issued_sgd 0.00 and charged_at null, so the fee stays on hold while review is pending. Your SGD 3.20 compensation (80% of SGD 4.00) is not paid. Per POL-NS-07 the reviewer is directed to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full if the escalation resolves in the rider's favour. The riders' and driver's remaining claims on the same points are answered together above: both sides' POL-NS-01 and POL-NS-02 claims are accepted, both sides' POL-NS-07 anti-farming and POL-NS-09(d) claims are accepted and are what decide this case, and the rider's point that the fee is held rather than collected is accepted. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00207-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is disclosed but carries no fact and is needed by no clause here, since the dwell already exceeds the minimum without accumulation. The profile fields rating, account_age_days, lifetime_trips, cancellation_rate, prior_disputes_filed, prior_no_show_flags and the like were raised only to be disclaimed as context-only under POL-GEN-01 and were not used as any ground of decision."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full; the fee is held under POL-NS-09 while review is pending."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this case goes to a human reviewer, and the SGD 4.00 no-show fee stays on hold while that happens — neither collected from the rider nor refunded — because EV-FARE-00207 records payment_status PENDING, charged_at null and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. Escalation is terminal, so no money moves under this ruling and the packet carries the review instruction below. Confidence is 0.90, above the platform floor of 0.70, and every fact the ruling rests on comes from an artifact at weight 1.0.\n\nOn the trip itself, the driver's account holds and the rider's does not. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00207 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 06:41:10 — ten seconds before the recorded arrival event at 06:41:20 (EV-TRIP-00207) — with 52 qualifying fixes, 100% coverage and no sampling gaps, and shows him holding position for 507 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum before cancelling at 06:49:37 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. All four conditions of POL-NS-01 (limbs a to d) are therefore satisfied, and none of the displacing clauses applies: POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) because the driver's stationary fixes are inside the arrival radius, not in the 50–400 m band; POL-NS-04 (rider contact unanswered) because the rider sent no message in EV-CHAT-00207 and the driver both messaged from 06:42:30 and placed an unanswered in-app call at 06:45:10; POL-NS-05 (false arrival marker) because at the marker the driver was within the geofence (closest approach 14.5 m) and stationary, not over 300 m away or moving at 15 km/h; and POL-NS-06 (waiting shortfall) because the measured dwell of 507 seconds exceeds the 300-second STANDARD minimum by 207 seconds. The charge itself reconciles: the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) is SGD 4.00, matching the fare breakdown's cancellation_fee line, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged.\n\nThe rider's claim that he 'came down, just a few minutes later' is not corroborated. His own device track in EV-GPS-00207 carries 118 fixes stationary roughly 1.9 km from the pin (between 1,894 m and 1,907 m) across the whole waiting window, with zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, and he wrote nothing in the chat log. His demand for the SGD 4.00 back fails on the merits of the trip.\n\nThe reason the fee does not simply stand, and the reason the driver recovers nothing despite being right about the trip, is POL-NS-07's anti-farming check, which runs on the driver's own profile and meets both of its limbs on EV-DPROF-00207: 7 no-show terminations in the trailing 30 days (the limb requires 4 or more) against 61 completed trips in the same window, a rate of 11.5% (the limb requires above 8%). POL-NS-07 therefore withholds the driver's SGD 3.20 (80% of the SGD 4.00 fee) and sends the case to escalation under POL-NS-09(d). I stress that this is a profile-based limit on the payout, not a finding against the driver on this trip, and that the rider's own side of the record is clean: the only rider-side counter this category reads, no_show_disputes_30d, stands at 1 (below the 3 that POL-NS-09(d) requires) and the parties show 0 disputes with each other in 90 days (POL-NS-09(c)). No other escalation limb is met, and confidence is not below the floor. The open question for the reviewer is the driver's 30-day no-show pattern, and the packet directs the reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation-fee line in full; the SGD 0.50 platform fee is not part of the contested amount."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07 — the escalation packet must DIRECT THE REVIEWER to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full; the SGD 4.00 is held meanwhile rather than collected or refunded by the automated pipeline."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. On the trip itself the driver is right and the rider is wrong. EV-GPS-00207 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 06:41:10 — ten seconds before his 06:41:20 'arrived' event — holding position in one unbroken 507-second run (52 qualifying fixes, 100% coverage, no sampling gaps) against the 300-second STANDARD minimum. EV-TRIP-00207 records the 06:49:37 termination by the driver with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW and no boarding event anywhere. POL-NS-01 limbs (a) to (d) are therefore satisfied in full, and nothing displaces them: not POL-NS-03 (the driver was at the pin itself, not in the 50–400 m wrong-entrance band), not POL-NS-04 (the rider sent no message at all in EV-CHAT-00207, and the driver both messaged from 06:42:30 and placed an unanswered in-app call at 06:45:10, so limbs (a) and (b) fail), not POL-NS-05 (closest approach about 14.5 m, no false marker), and not POL-NS-06 (a 507-second dwell leaves no shortfall, and the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00207-01 is not needed). The rider's own device track sits about 1.9 km from the pin for the entire window and returns no qualifying fix, so the claim to have 'come down a few minutes late' is contradicted by his own telemetry. The SGD 4.00 reconciles with the fee schedule — the GREATER of the SGD 4.00 STANDARD zone fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee — so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged and the fee is chargeable.

The outcome on the money is nevertheless an escalation, because of the driver's own 30-day record. POL-NS-07 compensates the driver at 80 percent of the fee, SGD 3.20, only if the anti-farming check does not trip. On EV-DPROF-00207 it trips on both limbs: 7 no-show terminations in the trailing 30 days is 4 or more, and 7 ÷ 61 completed trips is 0.115, above the 0.08 rate. Compensation is therefore withheld, and POL-NS-09(d) escalates the case. Escalation is terminal under POL-GEN-03: no money moves on this ruling, and the disputed SGD 4.00 is held, not collected and not refunded — EV-FARE-00207 shows payment_status PENDING, refund_issued_sgd 0.00 and no charge date. The SGD 0.50 platform fee is outside the contested amount.

Points taken. The rider's account of the trigger (7 terminations, 61 trips, 0.115), of the held fee, of the SGD 4.00 refund figure, and his concession that he was not at the pickup point are all accepted; his profile is used only as POL-GEN-01 allows — no_show_disputes_30d is 1 and disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0, and rating, account age, lifetime trips, prior disputes filed and prior_no_show_flags count for nothing. The driver's limb-by-limb POL-NS-01 case is accepted and he wins the merits of this trip, but his claim that he is owed SGD 3.20 and that the fee simply stands is not the outcome: the anti-farming check withholds the compensation, and the escalation displaces the ordinary fee disposition. It is his compensation, not the trip finding, that the profile affects. Escalation trigger: POL-NS-09(d) via the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check. Open question for the reviewer: whether the driver's trailing-30-day no-show pattern justifies the withholding, on which the packet carries POL-NS-07's direction that the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee be refunded in full."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
